Hi Ahnjili,

Yes the info Nate requested would be helpful. At the same time, I think it's mostly due to a problem in our current version. I believe the hBayesDM package will be installed smoothly on Mac and Linux computers. But it won't be installed on a Windows computer unless it has a lot of memory. It is because we included precompiled models in the latest version. Please check this out: https://github.com/CCS-Lab/hBayesDM/issues/13.

In a week or so, we will release a new version (0.4.0), separately on CRAN and GitHub. I believe you won't have an installation problem with the new version if you use CRAN, so please stay tuned.

Best,
Young

